<BaseLayout title="KD3 (Taixi) — Great Stream Point" description="Learn how to locate and stimulate KD3 (Taixi) — the Great Stream point. Benefits include kidney energy support, fatigue relief, and anxiety reduction." breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Points", href: "/points" }, { label: "KD3 (Taixi)", href: "/points/kd3-taixi-acupressure-point" }]} articleSchema={true}>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 lg:px-6">
    <h1 class="mb-4">KD3 (Taixi) — Great Stream</h1>
    <p class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 text-lg mb-8">KD3, known as Taixi or Great Stream, is the source point of the Kidney meridian. It is used for Kidney energy deficiency, chronic fatigue, anxiety, and lower back pain.</p>

    <section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Location</h2>
    <img src="/images/kd3-location.webp" alt="KD3 acupressure point location on the inner ankle" class="w-full max-w-sm mx-auto rounded-xl shadow-sm" />
    <p class="mb-3">KD3 is on the inner ankle, in the depression between the medial malleolus (inner ankle bone) and the Achilles tendon, level with the top of the ankle bone.</p>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Benefits &amp; Uses</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-1 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li><strong>Kidney energy:</strong> KD3 nourishes Kidney yin and yang, supporting adrenal function and vitality.</li>
      <li><strong>Chronic fatigue:</strong> It helps restore energy levels in those experiencing burnout or exhaustion.</li>
      <li><strong>Anxiety and fear:</strong> KD3 calms the mind and is used for anxiety rooted in fear or insecurity.</li>
      <li><strong>Lower back pain:</strong> It strengthens the lower back and is used for chronic lumbar weakness.</li>
      <li><strong>Bone and joint health:</strong> In traditional Chinese medicine, the Kidneys govern the bones ?KD3 supports bone density and joint health.</li>
    </ul>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">How to Massage KD3</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li>Sit with your leg comfortably positioned to access the inner ankle.</li>
      <li>Place your thumb on the KD3 point between the ankle bone and Achilles tendon.</li>
      <li>Apply firm, steady pressure with a gentle circular motion.</li>
      <li>Hold for 1— minutes, then switch to the other ankle.</li>
      <li>Repeat once or twice daily for best results.</li>
    </ol>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Science &amp; Research</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">A 2018 study in <em>Journal of Traditional Chinese Medicine</em> found that KD3 acupuncture improved kidney function markers in patients with chronic kidney disease.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30048947/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1</a></sup> Research in <em>Medicine</em> showed that KD3 stimulation reduced anxiety and improved sleep quality in peri-menopausal women.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32957376/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2</a></sup></p>
    <p class="mb-3">A 2020 fMRI study in <em>Brain Research</em> demonstrated that KD3 acupressure activates the insula and prefrontal cortex, areas associated with interoception and emotional regulation.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32335647/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3</a></sup></p>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Precautions</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-1 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li>Avoid if you have an ankle fracture, severe sprain, or infection in the area.</li>
      <li>Use gentle pressure ?the area between the ankle bone and tendon contains sensitive nerves.</li>
      <li>Do not massage over deep vein thrombosis or severe varicose veins.</li>
      <li>Stop if you experience sharp or shooting pain.</li>
    </ul>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Related Points</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">KD3 pairs well with <a href="/points/cv6-qihai-acupressure-point">CV6 (Qihai)</a> for overall Qi and Jing (essence) nourishment. For anxiety and insomnia, combine with <a href="/points/ht7-shenmen-acupressure-point">HT7 (Shenmen)</a> and <a href="/points/sp6-sanyinjiao-acupressure-point">SP6 (Sanyinjiao)</a>.</p>
  </section></article>
</BaseLayout>
